## What this predicate means

**A `has-beginning` B** — memorial A is an *occurrent* (session log, memoir, plan transition, authorization event, or other event-shaped memory) and B is its temporal beginning (a literal `xsd:date` / `xsd:dateTime` for now; eventually a `:mm/TimeInstant` reference when that type lands).  The OWL-Time interval-boundary axis applied to memorial occurrents.  Companion to `has-end` (which marks the occurrent's terminating boundary).  Functional — one beginning per occurrent.

